      "font_size": 11.84,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 92,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p25_b4",
      "text": "DRO protects absolute value and can therefore become conservative even when the proxy\nstill contains useful comparative information. DRRO protects regret, so its pessimism\nis relative to the policies that compete under the same plausible reward perturbation.\nThis section formalizes that difference through two lenses: rank preservation and local\ncoverage.\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.58,
        352.31,
        525.59,
        435.89
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        286,
        1409,
