      "font_size": 14.35,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Bold",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 33,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p25_b6",
      "text": "Pairwise reward-model training is fundamentally ordinal. Bradley\u2013Terry-style objectives\nand modern RLHF reward-model pipelines learn scores by assigning larger values to\npreferred responses than to rejected ones [Bradley and Terry, 1952, Christiano et al.,\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        488.58,
        524.95,
        536.4
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        1954,
        2099,
        2145
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.94,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 256,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p25_b7",
      "text": "2017, Stiennon et al., 2020, Ouyang et al., 2022]. This is why held-out pairwise accuracy\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.71,
        542.37,
        523.8,
        554.29
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        286,
        2169,
        2095,
